            "text": "City mornings begin as a watercolor wash, the cool blue of dawn leaching into the warmed edges of brick and glass. The tram clatters along its route, a gentle percussion that pulses beneath the way people move; each face a little story, a small constellation of hopes. I enjoy wandering, though I could follow a straight line, but I prefer the temptation of alleys echoing with laughter from caf\u00e9s that have been breathing coffee for decades. A stray dog trots beside a courier, they share a rhythm, a silent pact about the lengths they will go for Friday deliveries. In the park, a violin weaves through the leaves, a thin silk thread of sound that catches on benches and ripples into passing conversations. I might stop to watch a clumsy heron lift over the canal, wings wide and awkward until it becomes a graceful bird again. The weather shifts, dew evaporating into puddles that dazzle like coins thrown in air. Street vendors rearrange their trays, gloves on, breath visible and bright. Some people hurry to offices, others sit on stoops sipping tea, letting the city be a background score while they read. It is odd to think that in each window there is a different life, different reasons for whatever steps they take next. The city is a collective dream, layered and brilliant. At night, neon reflections stretch on wet streets, a reminder that even exhaustion can glow; the city keeps breathing, perhaps waiting for someone else to dream again."
